{
  "$schema": "./schema.json",
  "day": 19,
  "level": 2,
  "title": { "en": "I have", "es": "Tengo…" },
  "objectives": [
    "Use tengo, tienes and tiene to say what someone has",
    "Ask ¿Tienes…? to friends and ¿Tiene…? in a shop or bar",
    "Say you're hungry, thirsty, cold or hot with tener"
  ],
  "teach": [
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "**tener** means *to have*. Like *querer*, its stem changes to **tien-** in most forms. And *yo* is irregular: **tengo**, with a g."
    },
    {
      "kind": "conjugation",
      "verb": "tener",
      "verbEn": "to have",
      "tense": "present",
      "forms": {
        "yo": "tengo",
        "tu": "tienes",
        "el": "tiene",
        "nosotros": "tenemos",
        "vosotros": "tenéis",
        "ellos": "tienen"
      }
    },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "¿Tienes el móvil?", "en": "Have you got your phone?", "note": "Spanish uses el, not tu, when it's obvious whose it is." },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "¿Tiene agua sin gas?", "en": "Do you have still water?", "note": "Use tiene (usted) to a waiter or shop assistant. It's the normal way to ask if they sell or serve something." },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "**Spanish *has* hunger, thirst, cold and heat.** English says *I am hungry*; Spanish says *I have hunger*:\n\n- **tengo hambre**: I'm hungry\n- **tengo sed**: I'm thirsty\n- **tengo frío**: I'm cold\n- **tengo calor**: I'm hot\n\nDon't say ~~estoy frío~~. That describes something cold to the touch. For *very*, use **mucho** or **mucha**: *tengo mucho frío*, *tengo mucha hambre* (hambre is feminine).\n\nAge works the same way: *Tengo treinta años* = I'm thirty."
    },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "Tengo mucho frío.", "en": "I'm really cold.", "note": "You'll say this a lot in Madrid in January. Mornings are often around 0 °C." }
  ],
  "vocab": [
    { "id": "tener", "es": "tener", "en": "to have", "pos": "verb", "ipa": "teˈneɾ" },
    { "id": "tengo", "es": "tengo", "en": "I have", "pos": "verb", "ipa": "ˈteŋgo" },
    { "id": "tienes", "es": "tienes", "en": "you have", "pos": "verb", "ipa": "ˈtjenes", "note": "Informal tú. With usted: tiene." },
    { "id": "tiene", "es": "tiene", "en": "he / she has; you have (usted)", "pos": "verb", "ipa": "ˈtjene" },
    { "id": "tienes-q", "es": "¿Tienes…?, ¿Tiene…?", "en": "Do you have…?", "pos": "phrase", "ipa": "ˈtjenes, ˈtjene", "note": "¿Tienes…? to a friend, ¿Tiene…? to staff.", "tags": ["survival", "shopping"] },
    { "id": "tengo-hambre", "es": "tengo hambre", "en": "I'm hungry", "pos": "phrase", "ipa": "ˈteŋgo ˈambɾe", "note": "The h is silent.", "tags": ["survival"] },
    { "id": "tengo-sed", "es": "tengo sed", "en": "I'm thirsty", "pos": "phrase", "ipa": "ˈteŋgo ˈseð", "tags": ["survival"] },
    { "id": "tengo-frio", "es": "tengo frío", "en": "I'm cold", "pos": "phrase", "ipa": "ˈteŋgo ˈfɾio", "tags": ["survival"] },
    { "id": "tengo-calor", "es": "tengo calor", "en": "I'm hot", "pos": "phrase", "ipa": "ˈteŋgo kaˈloɾ" }
  ],
  "exercises": [
